## Recipe 6: WhatsApp Outbound Campaign (Template Setup)

Sets up a WhatsApp deployment with an approved message template, end-to-end.
This covers: channel setup → template creation → Meta approval → deployment → template attachment.

**CLI version (recommended — fastest path):**

```bash
# 1. Create agent
nexus agent create --first-name "Order" --last-name "Bot" --role "Customer notifications" --json

# 2. Set up WhatsApp channel (auto-provisions connection)
nexus channel setup --type WHATSAPP --auto

# 3. Connect WhatsApp Business Account (requires browser)
nexus channel connect-waba

# 4. Buy a phone number
nexus phone-number search --country US --sms
nexus phone-number buy --phone-number +12025551234 --country US --price 1.15 --json

# 5. Create WhatsApp sender
nexus channel whatsapp-sender create \
  --connection-id <connection-id> \
  --phone-number-id <phone-id> \
  --sender-name "My Business" --json

# 6. Verify readiness
nexus channel setup --type WHATSAPP

# 7. Create template + submit for approval in one step
nexus channel whatsapp-template create \
  --connection-id <connection-id> \
  --friendly-name order_confirmation \
  --language en \
  --body "Hi {{1}}, your order #{{2}} has been confirmed. Track at {{3}}" \
  --variables '{"1":"Customer","2":"12345","3":"https://example.com"}' \
  --submit --category UTILITY --json

# 8. Wait for approval (or poll manually)
nexus channel whatsapp-template approvals

# 9. Create WhatsApp deployment
nexus deployment create \
  --name "WhatsApp Notifications" \
  --type WHATSAPP \
  --agent-id <agent-id> \
  --body '{"whatsappSenderId":"<sender-id>"}' --json

# 10. Attach approved template to deployment
nexus deployment template attach <deployment-id> \
  --template-id <template-sid> \
  --name order_confirmation \
  --description "Sends order confirmation with tracking link" \
  --variables '{"1":{"description":"Customer name","isBodyVariable":true},"2":{"description":"Order number","isBodyVariable":true},"3":{"description":"Tracking URL","isBodyVariable":true}}'

# 11. Verify template is attached
nexus deployment template list <deployment-id>

# 12. Test via emulator
nexus emulator session create <deployment-id> --json
nexus emulator send <deployment-id> <session-id> --text "Send me my order status"
```

**Key points:**

- Step 3 requires a browser — cannot be automated via API
- Template approval (step 7-8) typically takes seconds for UTILITY, minutes for MARKETING
- The agent can now use the attached template when initiating outbound conversations
- Within a 24-hour customer-initiated conversation window, the agent can send free-form text
- After 24 hours of inactivity, templates are required again to re-initiate

